+/* GIMP - The GNU Image Manipulation Program
+ *
+ * file-pdf-chopgimp.h — ChopGimp 3.31.0 (lot 4b): vector PDF and EPS
+ * export. Included by file-pdf-export.c only (after its prototypes).
+ *
+ *  - the objects of ChopGimp's vector layers (XML of the PDB procedure
+ *    chopgimp-vobjects-get-xml, parsed by file-svg-vobjects.h, the SVG
+ *    export's code) are drawn with cairo as vectors: paths, groups with
+ *    their opacity and blend mode (PDF blend modes), clipping groups (PDF
+ *    clip), fills and strokes of every kind — plain colors, linear and
+ *    radial gradients (PDF shadings), « filets de dégradé » and
+ *    « dégradés libres » (PDF mesh shadings, as the model draws them),
+ *    vector patterns (PDF tiling patterns of the pattern's objects), GIMP
+ *    patterns (image tiles), stroke alignment, dashes, width profiles
+ *    (their outline), arrowheads; « masques d'opacité » (luminance) are
+ *    the one rasterized part (cairo has alpha masks only): the mask, not
+ *    the objects;
+ *  - text layers stay text (file-pdf-export's drawText: fonts embedded);
+ *  - layers keep their blend mode (PDF blend modes; the GIMP modes PDF
+ *    does not have use the nearest one), opacity, mask and groups;
+ *  - layers with effects (filters) were merged by the export options:
+ *    rasterized layer by layer, the « behind » effects (drop shadow, outer
+ *    glow in their own mode) as layers of their own under the layer;
+ *  - artboards (chopgimp-artboards-parse.h): the whole image, one page
+ *    per artboard, or one file per artboard (« -01-Nom.pdf »);
+ *  - PDF layers (OCG): each layer is drawn alone on a page of an
+ *    intermediate PDF 1.4, then the PDB procedure chopgimp-pdf-ocg-layers
+ *    (plug-in chopgimp_pdf, module ocg.py, no dependency) builds the
+ *    final pages: one optional content group per layer, groups nested
+ *    (opacity and blend mode as transparency groups), hidden layers off;
+ *    without that procedure, or if it fails, a PDF without layers;
+ *  - EPS (file-chopgimp-eps-export): the same drawing on a PostScript
+ *    surface in EPS mode, one file per artboard; cairo rasterizes what
+ *    PostScript cannot draw (transparency, blend modes).
+ *
+ * CHOPGIMP_NO_PDF_VECTOR=1: GIMP's PDF export, as before.
+ *
+ * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
+ * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
+ * the Free Software Foundation; either version 3 of the License, or
+ * (at your option) any later version.
+ */
